  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a permutation PPP, define f(P,K)f(P, K)f(P,K) in the following way:\n\n\nStart with an empty set of pairs SSS.\nYou can do the following action repeatedly as many times as you want:\n\nChoose 222 integers 1≤u&lt;v≤N1 \\le u &lt; v \\le N1≤u&lt;v≤N\nSwap PuP_uPu​ and PvP_vPv​\nAdd (u,v)(u, v)(u,v) to our set SSS\n\n\nWhen PPP is sorted, we define the scorescorescore to be ∑(u+v+K)\\sum(u + v + K)∑(u+v+K) for distinct (u,v)(u, v)(u,v) in the set SSS\nf(P)f(P)f(P) is the minimum possible score to obtain a sorted permutation.\nYou are given integers NNN and KKK. Find the sum of f(P)f(P)f(P) over all permutations of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N]. Since the answer may be large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of f(P)f(P)f(P) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "0≤K≤N≤2⋅1050 \\le K \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^50≤K≤N≤2⋅105",
      "2≤N2 \\le N2≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
